{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a0e1f0841876b943a155d6140803c121db2d09c35f15efaae5a2f612523dfae8","digest":{"component_or_area":"git contention seam test","key_entities":["tests/interfaces/store/test_git_contention_9305.py::test_concurrent_processes_through_seam_both_succeed","rebar._store.gitutil","run_git_write","_with_index_lock_retry","git commit","git add"],"problem_keywords":["flaky test","git contention","race condition","concurrent writers","index lock","shared state"],"propositions":["Two concurrent workers racing on a shared git index can produce an interleaving where one worker's commit is a no-op because the other worker's commit swept up both changes.","The test assertion for commit returncode==0 is violated when git commit returns rc=1 with empty stderr due to 'nothing to commit' after index was swept by concurrent writer.","Each run_git_write call acquires the lock independently, so the add/commit pair is not serialized and permits the index-race interleaving.","The test must commit each writer's own pathspec rather than the whole index to guarantee each commit is non-empty regardless of interleaving order."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787484506718125001,"uuid":"9e5ccbed-a0a6-4223-a724-bb315a603696"}